INSERT INTO `scholarship_applications` VALUES
(11,28,1,1,'submitted','','Your most promising options are the CHED Tulong Dunong Program (TDP), the DNSC Academic Scholarship, the DNSC Student Assistant program, and the GrabScholar College Scholarship. These match your academic standing and financial background without demanding specific courses or specialized backgrounds like agriculture or fisheries. To move forward, your best next steps are to visit the DNSC Scholarship and Grants Unit to check the status of active scholarship calls and to secure a Barangay Certificate of Indigency to support your financial need applications.','2026-11-19 04:37:28','done','2026-11-19 04:37:28','gemini-3.5-flash-lite','2026-11-19 04:37:18','2026-11-19 04:37:18','2026-11-19 04:37:28'),
(12,33,1,0,'submitted','',NULL,NULL,'pending',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-19 06:46:00','2026-11-19 06:46:00','2026-11-19 07:01:27'),
(13,33,2,1,'updated','','Your profile is a strong match for government financial assistance programs that account for your background and current enrollment. The most promising options are the CHED Tertiary Education Subsidy (TES), where your 4Ps membership makes you eligible, and the Scholarship Program for Coconut Farmers and Their Families (CoScho), where your parent\'s registration with the PCA qualifies you. Both programs support your current studies without conflicting rules. \n\nYour immediate next steps should be to check with the DNSC financial aid office regarding your TES processing status. For the CoScho grant, you should immediately request your PCA certification and obtain a certified true copy of your college grades to prepare your application packet.','2026-11-19 07:01:45','done','2026-11-19 07:01:45','gemini-3.5-flash-lite','2026-11-19 07:01:27','2026-11-19 07:01:27','2026-11-19 07:01:45'),
(14,36,1,1,'submitted','',NULL,NULL,'failed',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-19 08:00:38','2026-11-19 08:00:38','2026-11-19 08:01:08'),
(15,44,1,1,'submitted','','Your most promising options are the DNSC Grant-in-Aid (GIA) Category A, since you have verified skills and awards in dance and sports, and the DNSC Student Assistant Category C, given your financial background and willingness to work. You may also want to explore the internal DNSC Academic Scholarship once you confirm your GWA against their specific cut-off. Most national government and private scholarships are unavailable to you right now because you are already in your second year, are past the normal program length, or do not match specific farmer or first-year criteria.\n\nFor your next steps, visit the DNSC Scholarship and Grants Unit to apply directly for the GIA Category A and Student Assistant positions. Be sure to bring your latest grades, Certificate of Registration, student ID, and any documentation of your dance or sports achievements to support your applications.','2026-11-19 20:57:17','done','2026-11-19 20:57:17','gemini-3.5-flash-lite','2026-11-19 20:57:08','2026-11-19 20:57:08','2026-11-19 20:57:17'),
(16,46,1,1,'submitted','','Your profile is a strong match for several merit and government-backed grants. The most promising opportunities include the CHED Merit Scholarship Program (CMSP), Bagong Pilipinas Merit Scholarship Program (BPMSP), GrabScholar, Cebuana Lhuillier Foundation National Scholarship, and CHED Tertiary Education Subsidy (TES), where your high grades, IT program, and solo parent status work in your favor.\n\nTo move forward, your best next steps are to prepare key documents such as your Grade 12 report card (Form 138), Certificate of Registration, and proof of income. You should also coordinate directly with the DNSC Scholarship Unit to monitor application windows for CHED and internal grants.','2026-11-19 21:16:34','done','2026-11-19 21:16:34','gemini-3.5-flash-lite','2026-11-19 21:16:26','2026-11-19 21:16:26','2026-11-19 21:16:34'),
(17,48,1,0,'submitted','','Based on your application, the most promising opportunities for you are the CHED Merit Scholarship Program (CMSP) and the Bagong Pilipinas Merit Scholarship Program (BPMSP), as your high Grade 12 average of 95.9% and family income comfortably meet their strict academic and financial rules. You also show good potential for the GrabScholar and Cebuana Lhuillier Foundation scholarships, though you should confirm if your Tourism Management program fits their accepted course lists. For your next steps, prepare your official senior high school report card, birth certificate, and proof of family income. Then, check with the DNSC Scholarship and Grants Unit or CHED Regional Office XI regarding application deadlines and portals for CMSP and BPMSP.','2026-11-20 18:50:49','done','2026-11-20 18:50:49','gemini-3.5-flash-lite','2026-11-20 18:50:39','2026-11-20 18:50:39','2026-11-21 02:53:47'),
(18,50,1,1,'submitted','','Your profile as a second-year BS Information Technology student at DNSC with a solid GWA of 1.43 and family income below ₱300k makes you a promising candidate for internal institutional assistance and government grants. The DNSC Academic Scholarship, DNSC Student Assistant Category C, and the CHED Tulong Dunong Program (TDP) offer the best potential matches.\n\nTo move forward, visit the DNSC Scholarship and Grants Unit to verify the internal GWA requirements and inquire about student assistant openings. Additionally, prepare your Barangay Certificate of Indigency so you are ready when the next CHED TDP application cycle opens.','2026-11-20 19:33:59','done','2026-11-20 19:33:59','gemini-3.5-flash-lite','2026-11-20 19:33:45','2026-11-20 19:33:45','2026-11-20 19:33:59'),
(19,43,1,0,'submitted','','Based on your academic background as a second-year IT student at DNSC with a high GWA, the most promising options for you are the DNSC Academic Scholarship, the DNSC Student Assistant (SA) – Category C, and the CHED Tulong Dunong Program (TDP). These opportunities align well with your financial background and current enrollment status, provided you meet their specific institutional cut-offs.\n\nYour immediate next steps should be to visit the DNSC Scholarship and Grants Unit to confirm the GWA requirement for the academic scholarship and inquire about student assistant openings. Additionally, you should prepare to secure a Certificate of Indigency from your barangay in anticipation of a CHED TDP application call.','2026-11-21 02:24:57','done','2026-11-21 02:24:57','gemini-3.5-flash-lite','2026-11-21 02:24:44','2026-11-21 02:24:44','2026-11-21 02:29:54'),
(20,43,2,1,'updated','','Your academic record is exceptional, featuring a Grade 12 average of 99 percent and a Top 5 class standing, which makes you a strong candidate for government merit grants. The CHED Merit Scholarship Program (CMSP) and the Bagong Pilipinas Merit Scholarship Program (BPMSP) look most promising because you meet all academic and income requirements for both. Other options like the DNSC Academic Scholarship and CHED Tulong Dunong Program are also worth exploring.\n\nFor your next steps, you should prepare your official Grade 12 report card, proof of family income, and your birth certificate. Visit the DNSC Scholarship and Grants Unit to confirm application deadlines and check if your program qualifies for additional regional priorities.','2026-11-21 02:30:03','done','2026-11-21 02:30:03','gemini-3.5-flash-lite','2026-11-21 02:29:54','2026-11-21 02:29:54','2026-11-21 02:30:03'),
(21,48,2,1,'updated','','Your strongest opportunities are the CHED Merit Scholarship Program (CMSP) and the Bagong Pilipinas Merit Scholarship Program (BPMSP), where your high school average of 95.9%, Top 5 class standing, and low family income make you fully eligible to apply. You also show good potential for the CHED Tulong Dunong Program (TDP), GrabScholar, and the Cebuana Lhuillier Foundation Scholarship, though you will need to check specific course alignments or secure a barangay indigency certificate.\n\nYour immediate next steps should be to prepare your Grade 12 report card, birth certificate, and proof of family income. Then, reach out to the DNSC Scholarship and Grants Unit or check the CHED regional office portal to confirm application deadlines and process your submissions for CMSP and BPMSP.','2026-11-21 03:53:11','done','2026-11-21 03:53:11','gemini-3.5-flash-lite','2026-11-21 02:53:47','2026-11-21 02:53:47','2026-11-21 03:53:11');
